# Foundation HTML Conventions

Project-specific markup deltas only. For generic HTML5, semantic elements, form
inputs, and ARIA reference, use [MDN](mdc:https://developer.mozilla.org).

## ID Naming Convention

Use `CamelCase` for IDs and always append the section/block identifier — these
are the only values guaranteed unique on the page.

```html
<section id="FeaturedCollection-{{ section.id }}">
<div id="ProductCard-{{ block.id }}">
<dialog id="ProductModal-{{ product.id }}-{{ section.id }}">
<form id="ProductForm-{{ product.id }}-{{ section.id }}">
```

## Custom Elements

Prefer native HTML where it suffices. Where the theme needs animation, focus
trapping, or global state, use these registered custom elements instead of
inline scripts.

**Quick shop** — wraps a trigger; the quickshop dialog is rendered/handled
globally (state in [modal store](mdc:src/stores/modal.ts)), markup in
[snippets/quickshop.liquid](mdc:snippets/quickshop.liquid). Element:
[`<quick-shop-toggle>`](mdc:src/entry/core/core-quickshop-toggle.ts).

```html
<quick-shop-toggle product-url="{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url | within: collection }}">
  <button class="product__quick-view">{{ 'products.quick_view' | t }}</button>
</quick-shop-toggle>
```

**Modal dialog** — [`<dialog-toggle modal-id="...">`](mdc:src/components/dialog-toggle.ts)
opens the matching [`<modal-dialog>`](mdc:src/entry/core/core-dialog.ts). The
`modal-id` must match the dialog's `id` (include `-{{ section.id }}`).

```html
<dialog-toggle modal-id="ProductModal-{{ product.id }}-{{ section.id }}">
  <button class="product__details-toggle">{{ 'products.details' | t }}</button>
</dialog-toggle>

<modal-dialog id="ProductModal-{{ product.id }}-{{ section.id }}">
  ...
</modal-dialog>
```

**Accordion** — use [`<custom-accordion>`](mdc:src/entry/core/core-accordion.ts)
where the open/close needs animation; plain `<details>`/`<summary>` otherwise.

## No Inline Event Handlers

Never use `onclick`, `onsubmit`, `onload`, etc. Wrap interactive markup in a
custom element and handle events there (event delegation), not in attributes.
